course: dictionary
lesson: 4498
title: Many jobs of one small word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The word have is small, but it does many jobs. It can mean to own something, as in «I have a bike». It can also be a helper word that makes past tenses, as in «I have finished». Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing.
explain: Have to means must. In «Alice has to run off to hide her laughter», has to means Alice must run off. Phrases like have a go, have a look and have lunch work as a set, so learn them together instead of changing each word on its own.
explain: Have can also mean to be made of or contain, as in «A week has 7 days», or to get an illness, as in «I have a cold». The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Have means to own or hold something: I have a bike.
fact: Have to means must: «Alice has to run off» means she must run off.
fact: Have helps make past tenses: I have finished, she has finished.
fact: Have can mean to eat, drink or take part in something: have lunch, have a bath, have a test.
fact: Use has with he, she and it, and have with I, you, we and they.
exercise: «A boy in Halifax has an eye test.» In this sentence, what does has mean? | To own a pet | *To take part in, as in have a test | To make the past tense | To be made of
exercise: «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies.» What does have mean here? | To pay for | *To be made of | To eat | To get ill
exercise: In «Alice has to run off to hide her laughter», what does has to mean? | *Must | To own something | To eat | To be ill with
test: In «some children have spent hundreds without their parents knowing», what job does have do? | To be ill with | To own something | *To make the past tense, as in have spent | To must
test: Which sentence uses have to mean must? | I have finished my tea. | I have a bike. | A week has 7 days. | *I have to go now.
exam: Which sentence uses have to mean own or hold? | *I have a bike and a dog | I have finished my homework | I have to go home | I have a cold
